ls","sh"],["hs","ns"],["hs","ss"],["hs","es"],["at","If East has the @SK then South can win a twelfth trick by leading toward his @SQ. "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["ls","ss"],["ls","es"],["md","0,sk,,d9"],["hs","ed"],["hs","wd"],["hs","nd"],["hs","sd"],["at","Alternatively, a 3-2 diamond break could provide South with the extra trick that he needs. "],["pg",""],["ls","nd"],["ls","sd"],["ls","ed"],["md","0,d9,,s9"],["hs","ws"],["nt","Furthermore, South may be able to succeed with a squeeze if either defender (presumably West) was dealt 4 diamonds and the @SK. "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","wd"],["hs","sd"],["at","South may be tempted to allow West's diamond opening lead to win in an effort to rectify the count for a possible squeeze. "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["ls","sd"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pc","d"],["pg",""],["hs","ws"],["at","West can shift to a spade, however, "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["pc","sj"],["hs","ns"],["at","and South won't know if he should win dummy's @SA or not. "],["pg",""],["nt","If the @SA is played, "],["pg",""],["ls","ns"],["pc","sa"],["pc","s"],["pc","s"],["pg",""],["hs","ws"],["hs","wd"],["hs","sd"],["hs","ss"],["at","it will be impossible to squeeze West (as he is sitting over both South's spades and diamonds). "],["pg",""],["up","3"],["ls","ws"],["ls","ss"],["ls","wd"],["ls","sd"],["md","0,s9s8,,d9sk"],["hs","ns"],["hs","es"],["hs","ed"],["hs","wd"],["at","If instead South plays a low spade from dummy, he will go down when East was dealt the @SK and diamonds were 3-2. "],["pg",""],["up","2"],["md","0,d9sk,,s98"],["ls","wd"],["ls","ed"],["ls","ns"],["ls","es"],["hs","sd"],["nt","South must resist the temptation to duck the first trick. He should win West's diamond opening lead, "],["pg",""],["ls","sd"],["pc","da"],["pg",""],["hs","nh"],["hs","sh"],["at","unblock the hearts, "],["pg",""],["ls","nh"],["ls","sh"],["pc","hk"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["pc","hq"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pc","h"],["pg",""],["hs","sd"],["at","and test